rem Writing 1/2 as a Sum of Inverse
rem Squares
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=152
rem Count the sets of distinct integers
rem from 2 to Limit whose inverse
rem squares sum to 1/2

use algo
use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 80

rem Only numbers made of 2, 3, 5, 7, 13
rem can occur. For p = 13, 7, 5 the
rem chosen multiples of p must have a
rem sum free of p in the denominator;
rem drop those in no such set. Then meet
rem in the middle over the rest. The
rem Base is 2^6 3^3 5^2 7^2 13.
Ns = 2 to Limit array
Base = 27518400
Div = Base mod Ns equal 0
Cand = Ns filter Div array
Sq = Cand * Cand
L = Sq lcm
for Pr in array 13 7 5
  Pk = L (Pr ** 20) gcd
  Mul = Cand mod Pr equal 0
  Ms = Cand filter Mul array
  K = Ms len
  Size = 2 ** K
  Seq = 0 till Size array
  Mk = Seq reshape Size 1
  Bt = Mk (0 till K array) bit
  Vals = L // (Ms * Ms)
  Sums = (Bt choose Vals 0) sum axis 1
  Good = Sums mod Pk equal 0
  Used = (Bt (Good indices)) any axis 0
  Keep = Ms filter Used array
  Free = Cand mod Pr not equal 0
  Ok = Free or Cand in Keep
  Cand = Cand filter Ok array
end
Vals = L // (Cand * Cand)
Half = Cand len // 2
Left = array 0
for V in Vals take Half
  Left = concat Left (Left + V)
end
Right = array 0
for V in Vals drop Half
  Right = concat Right (Right + V)
end
Seen = new counter Right
Hits = Seen (L // 2 - Left)
Answer = Hits sum
Answer print
